---
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-CA">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <SEO
      title="About the Author — Badreddine Br"
      description="Meet Badreddine Br, the writer behind SmallSpace Home — a Toronto renter testing real small-apartment storage and decor solutions since 2023."
      path="/author"
      type="website"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-N5MCBQG6"
    height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript>
    <Header />

    <main class="author-page">
      <section class="author-hero">
        <div class="author-hero-inner">
          <div class="author-avatar-circle">
            <span class="author-initials">BB</span>
          </div>
          <span class="section-eyebrow">Written By</span>
          <h1 class="author-heading">Badreddine Br</h1>
          <p class="author-sub">Toronto renter · 510 sq ft apartment · Writing since 2023</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="author-body">
        <div class="author-inner">

          <div class="author-block">
            <h2>Background</h2>
            <p>
              I've lived in a 510 sq ft Toronto apartment for three years. Before starting SmallSpace
              Home, I spent months trying to make the space work using advice built for houses with
              basements and garages — none of it translated to a small Canadian rental where you can't
              drill into the walls and every square foot has to earn its place.
            </p>
            <p>
              I'm not a professional interior designer or organizer. What I bring is direct, repeated
              experience testing storage systems, furniture, and layouts in a real rental — and being
              honest in writing about what actually held up and what fell apart after a month.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="author-block">
            <h2>What I actually do for this site</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Test products in my own apartment before recommending them — prices and availability checked against Canadian retailers (IKEA Canada, Amazon.ca, HomeSense, Wayfair Canada, Canadian Tire, Structube)</li>
              <li>Write every guide from a renter's constraints: no drilling, no permanent changes, real CAD budgets</li>
              <li>Update posts when prices or product availability change, rather than leaving stale information live</li>
              <li>Reply personally to every message sent through <a href="/contact">the contact page</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="author-block">
            <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
            <p>
              Full detail on how content here gets researched, written, and corrected is on the
              <a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial Policy page</a>. Short version: real testing where
              possible, accurate Canadian pricing always, and no sponsored placements dressed up as
              genuine recommendations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="author-cta">
            <a href="/blog" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Blog →</a>
            <a href="/contact" class="btn">Get in Touch</a>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.author-page { padding-bottom: 0; }

.author-hero {
  background: var(--color-surface);
  padding: 80px 24px 56px;
  text-align: center;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
}
.author-hero-inner { max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; }
.author-avatar-circle {
  width: 88px;
  height: 88px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--color-ink);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  margin: 0 auto 24px;
}
.author-initials {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 1.3rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: #fff;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}
.section-eyebrow {
  font-size: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-accent-dark);
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.author-heading {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--color-ink);
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  line-height: 1.1;
}
.author-sub {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  margin: 0;
}

.author-body { background: var(--color-white); padding: 72px 24px 96px; }
.author-inner { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; }
.author-block { margin-bottom: 44px; }
.author-block:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }
.author-block h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: var(--color-ink);
  margin: 0 0 16px;
}
.author-block p {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
  margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
}
.author-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.author-block a { color: var(--color-accent-dark); }
.author-block ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 1.3rem;
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
.author-block ul li {
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.85;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
.author-cta {
  display: flex;
  gap: 16px;
  margin-top: 48px;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .author-hero { padding: 56px 20px 40px; }
  .author-body { padding: 48px 20px 64px; }
  .author-cta { flex-direction: column; }
}
</style>
